        "title": "About Condition Hurricane Storm",
        "subject": "Condition Hurricane Storm",
        "summary": "Hurricane Isaias is an Atlantic tropical cyclone in the Gulf of America, tracked by the U.S. National Hurricane Center (NHC) as AL092026. It formed as Tropical Depression Nine on October 6, 2026, became Tropical Storm Isaias on October 7, and strengthened into a major hurricane while approaching the northern Gulf Coast.",
        "facts": [
          {
            "label": "Formation and name",
            "value": "The system became Tropical Depression Nine over the Gulf of America at 4:00 PM CDT on October 6, 2026, and was named Tropical Storm Isaias at 4:00 AM CDT on October 7.",
            "source_ids": [
              "o1",
              "o2"
            ]
          },
          {
            "label": "Monitoring authority",
            "value": "The National Hurricane Center, part of the U.S. National Weather Service, issues the storm’s official advisories, forecasts, and U.S. coastal watch and warning products.",
