              "o4"
            ]
          },
          {
            "label": "Status on October 9, 2026",
            "value": "At 11:00 AM CDT on October 9, Isaias had maximum sustained winds of 120 mph and a central pressure of 959 mb, placing it in Category 3—the “major hurricane” range—on the Saffir-Simpson Hurricane Wind Scale.",
            "source_ids": [
              "o5",
              "o6"
            ]
          },
          {
            "label": "Location and movement",
            "value": "At that update, the center was about 180 miles south of Pensacola, Florida, moving north-northeast at 16 mph toward the western Florida Panhandle and Alabama coast.",
